  "notes": "Drawn from right-side photos only (C-GPFT 2024, C-FNWD 2025) and mirrored: the left side should match. The fin's facets are simplified to two areas. WestJet Encore (WEN) wears this scheme. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on C-GPFT (flipped, fitted to the measured 737-800 shape, whose fuselage the MAX 8 shares): the title's baseline is just under the windows' middle (about 0.3 m below it, y 0.085) and its capitals stand about 0.77 m above it (height 0.40; it had been drawn reaching most of the way to the crown); x 0.16 to 0.37 as drawn. The teal's front edge is straight from the side: drawn by its two ends. The fin's facets stay simplified (the white is a dotted gradient on the aircraft). WestJet's 737-800s, its commonest type, wear the same layout.",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximate standard (a few colors from memory). The 2018 livery replaced WestJet's teal-and-blue 'tail' scheme of the 2000s."
